  </section>

  <section class="speed">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head">
        <h2>A new worktree is ready in seconds</h2>
        <p class="lede">No reinstall. No dump and restore. <code>berth add</code> clones what your branch needs and hands the terminal back while the big copies finish in the background.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tiers">
        <div>
          <span class="fig">Instant</span>
          <b>Ports, names and <code>.env</code></b>
          <p>Assigned and written the moment you run <code>berth add</code>, however large the project.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="fig">0.5 s</span>
          <b><code>node_modules/</code> and <code>vendor/</code></b>
          <p>30,000 files cloned copy-on-write, so there is nothing to reinstall and almost no extra disk used.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="fig">1.6 s</span>
          <b>A 1 GB Postgres database</b>
          <p>Cloned inside the server on Postgres 18. Your branch gets real data to migrate, and main's stays as it was.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="more"><a href="/docs/background/performance/">See how berth copies each kind of data</a></p>
      <p class="safety"><b>And safe with your data.</b> Berth never starts your services, never changes main's data, and deletes only what it created. <a href="/docs/reference/guarantees/">Read the guarantees</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="start" id="start">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div>
        <h2>Set it up once, then forget it's there</h2>
        <p class="lede">One binary, one command per repo. Your app, your scripts and your compose file stay exactly as they are.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step wide">
          <div class="os" role="tablist" aria-label="Platform">
            <button type="button" role="tab" data-os="unix" aria-selected="true">macOS and Linux</button>
            <button type="button" role="tab" data-os="windows" aria-selected="false">Windows</button>
            <button type="button" role="tab" data-os="go" aria-selected="false">Go</button>
          </div>
          <pre id="install-cmd"><span class="pr">$</span> curl -fsSL https://useberth.dev/install | sh</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="step"><span>Once per repo</span><pre><span class="pr">$</span> berth init</pre></div>
        <div class="step"><span>When a worktree needs to run</span><pre><span class="pr">$</span> git worktree add .worktrees/x
<span class="pr">$</span> cd .worktrees/x &amp;&amp; berth add
<span class="pr">$</span> npm run dev</pre></div>
        <div class="step"><span>Or make it automatic for every worktree</span><pre><span class="pr">$</span> berth hook install</pre></div>
      </div>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn primary" href="https://github.com/kodnificent/berth">View on GitHub</a>
        <a class="btn secondary" href="/docs/quickstart/">Read the docs</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

